{"t": 265.23, "kind": "proposal", "iteration": 1, "k": 1, "move": "new_topology", "name": "SSHI_FullBridge", "rationale": "The open-circuit voltage of the piezo (~0.76V) is lower than the required load voltage (1.8V). A standard SSHI (Synchronous Switch Harvesting on Inductor) topology is used to invert the voltage across the piezo capacitance at each peak, effectively boosting the voltage to a level that can overcome the diode drops of a full-bridge rectifier and charge the storage capacitor to 1.8V. A Zener diode is added to clamp the output at 3.3V to prevent exceeding the absolute maximum of 3.6V.", "circuit": {"move": "new_topology", "name": "SSHI_FullBridge", "rationale": "The open-circuit voltage of the piezo (~0.76V) is lower than the required load voltage (1.8V). A standard SSHI (Synchronous Switch Harvesting on Inductor) topology is used to invert the voltage across the piezo capacitance at each peak, effectively boosting the voltage to a level that can overcome the diode drops of a full-bridge rectifier and charge the storage capacitor to 1.8V. A Zener diode is added to clamp the output at 3.3V to prevent exceeding the absolute maximum of 3.6V.", "done": false, "components": [{"id": "L1", "type": "L", "nodes": ["pzp", "n1"], "value": 0.01}, {"id": "S1", "type": "S", "nodes": ["n1", "pzn"], "ctrl": "G1"}, {"id": "G1", "type": "SYNC", "ton": 5e-05, "phase": 0.0, "edges": "both"}, {"id": "D1", "type": "D", "nodes": ["pzp", "out"], "model": "DSCH"}, {"id": "D2", "type": "D", "nodes": ["pzn", "out"], "model": "DSCH"}, {"id": "D3", "type": "D", "nodes": ["0", "pzp"], "model": "DSCH"}, {"id": "D4", "type": "D", "nodes": ["0", "pzn"], "model": "DSCH"}, {"id": "C1", "type": "C", "nodes": ["out", "0"], "value": 2.2e-06}, {"id": "DZ1", "type": "D", "nodes": ["0", "out"], "model": "DZ33"}]}}
