{"t": 495.22, "kind": "proposal", "iteration": 2, "k": 1, "move": "new_topology", "name": "SECE_Dual", "rationale": "The previous SSHI_FullBridge had sufficient power but suffered from high diode drops and poor voltage regulation, leading to failures in vavg (on weak excitation), startup time, and ripple. I am proposing a Synchronous Electric Charge Extraction (SECE) topology. SECE uses a resonant transfer (L-S) to move charge from the piezo to the storage capacitor, which inherently provides a voltage boost and avoids the forward voltage drops of a diode bridge. By using two symmetric branches for pzp and pzn, we capture energy from both half-cycles. This should increase the output voltage above 1.8V even for S4, S5, and S6, and by tuning L and C1, we can balance the startup speed and ripple requirements.", "circuit": {"move": "new_topology", "name": "SECE_Dual", "rationale": "The previous SSHI_FullBridge had sufficient power but suffered from high diode drops and poor voltage regulation, leading to failures in vavg (on weak excitation), startup time, and ripple. I am proposing a Synchronous Electric Charge Extraction (SECE) topology. SECE uses a resonant transfer (L-S) to move charge from the piezo to the storage capacitor, which inherently provides a voltage boost and avoids the forward voltage drops of a diode bridge. By using two symmetric branches for pzp and pzn, we capture energy from both half-cycles. This should increase the output voltage above 1.8V even for S4, S5, and S6, and by tuning L and C1, we can balance the startup speed and ripple requirements.", "done": false, "components": [{"id": "L1", "type": "L", "nodes": ["pzp", "n1"], "value": 0.001}, {"id": "S1", "type": "S", "nodes": ["n1", "out"], "ctrl": "G1"}, {"id": "G1", "type": "SYNC", "ton": 1e-05, "phase": 0.0, "edges": "pos"}, {"id": "L2", "type": "L", "nodes": ["pzn", "n2"], "value": 0.001}, {"id": "S2", "type": "S", "nodes": ["n2", "out"], "ctrl": "G2"}, {"id": "G2", "type": "SYNC", "ton": 1e