{"t": 736.92, "kind": "proposal", "iteration": 3, "k": 1, "move": "new_topology", "name": "Dual_Path_SECE", "rationale": "The previous SSHI_FullBridge design failed on S4 (weakest excitation) because the two-diode drop of the full-bridge rectifier reduced the output voltage too much. I am proposing a Dual-Path Synchronized Electric Charge Extraction (SECE) topology. This design uses two separate extraction paths (one for the positive peak, one for the negative peak) to pump charge from the piezo into the storage capacitor via inductors. By using individual return-path diodes, we reduce the voltage drop to a single diode per half-cycle and leverage the L-C resonance to boost the output voltage above the 1.8 V threshold even under weak excitation. I've also increased the storage capacitor to 1 uF to eliminate the ripple issues seen in S3.", "circuit": {"move": "new_topology", "name": "Dual_Path_SECE", "rationale": "The previous SSHI_FullBridge design failed on S4 (weakest excitation) because the two-diode drop of the full-bridge rectifier reduced the output voltage too much. I am proposing a Dual-Path Synchronized Electric Charge Extraction (SECE) topology. This design uses two separate extraction paths (one for the positive peak, one for the negative peak) to pump charge from the piezo into the storage capacitor via inductors. By using individual return-path diodes, we reduce the voltage drop to a single diode per half-cycle and leverage the L-C resonance to boost the output voltage above the 1.8 V threshold even under weak excitation. I've also increased the storage capacitor to 1 uF to eliminate the ripple issues seen in S3.", "done": false, "components": [{"id": "S1", "type": "S", "nodes": ["pzp", "n1"], "ctrl": "G1"}, {"id": "L1", "type": "L", "nodes": ["n1", "out"], "value": 0.001}, {"id": "G1", "type": "SYNC", "ton": 2e-05, "phase": 0.0, "edges": "pos"}, {"id": "S2", "type": "S", "nodes": ["pzn", "n2"], "ctrl": "G2"}, {"id": "L2", "type": "L", "nodes": ["n2", "